# Implementation stewardship（builder）

**Do** = application source per **AGENTS.md**, bounded by `.agents/plans/`.  
Default unit = **one factor** (or smallest combination) — [`docs/DESIGN_SEMANTICS.md`](../docs/DESIGN_SEMANTICS.md).

## When to use

- Plan exists with clear **Scope**, **Factors**, and **Acceptance criteria**
- User asks to **implement**, **build**, **code**, **add feature**
- Multi-file / multi-criterion Do within plan **Scope** (still prefer one factor per TDD cycle)
- After `plan_slicer`; before `reviewer` **Check**

**Not here**（→ **`hotfixer`**）: post-Do bugfix, tiny tweak within patch caps.

## Skills

| Purpose | Use |
|---------|-----|
| Context | `implement-reference` |
| Build | `implement-conduct` |
| PDCA Do log | `implement-record` |
| Checkpoint / criterion commit | `git-reference` → `git-record`（`docs/GIT_WORKFLOW.md`） |
| Role | **`builder`** |

## Hand off

| Next | Role |
|------|------|
| Check | `reviewer` |
| Plan change | `plan_slicer` |
| Spec gap | `spec_designer` |
| Progress review | `evaluator` |
| Small post-Do fix | `hotfixer` |

## vs PM

PM does not patch source inline. Use **`builder`** for plan-bound Do; **`hotfixer`** for small fixes.
